-- title:
--   Original BV cofinal negative-mark compensated signed grid has an integrable nonpositive-mean witness
-- statement:
--   For the original spectrally negative Lévy process X and arbitrary admissible singular dividend D, under BV, generator and discount conditions, construct cofinal positive spatial bands and the exact stopped intrinsic compensated negative-jump sum on each uniform deterministic time grid. With the supplementary signed drift B equal to zero, the physical jump-grid correction is integrable and its expectation is nonpositive. This supplies a source-faithful signed-budget component for the BV infinite-activity cell/contact error route, leaving the physical pathwise payoff bound and error convergence separately to be proved.
-- source:
--   Direct original-source specialisation of independently Proved avram_p3_comp8_original_cofinal_compensator_plus_signed_B, with B=0.

